course: dictionary
lesson: 9832
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: «Swift» usually means fast, but it is a stronger, more storybook word than fast. In «a swift horse» or «swift action», it means quick, with no delay. Context helps you choose the meaning: look at the words around it.
explain: «Swift» has a second meaning: it is the name of a bird. Read «swifts scream over the chimneys in summer». Chimneys are high up and birds can scream, so swifts here are birds. A word can mean different things, and the sentence decides which one.
explain: Capital letters are clues too. «Taylor Swift re-recorded her early albums» has a capital S after a first name, so Swift is a person's name, not a word for fast. Always ask: what does this word fit with, and does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Swift» means very fast, quick in moving.
fact: «Swift» can also mean happening quickly or without delay, as in «a swift reply».
fact: A swift is a small, fast bird with long pointed wings. Common swifts are thought to sleep while flying high up.
fact: A capital letter, as in «Taylor Swift», can show a name, so the word means a person, not a speed.
exercise: «The swift horse galloped across the field.» What does swift mean here? | Very wet | Very old | Very sleepy | *Very fast
exercise: «Common swifts can stay in the air for about ten months without landing.» What is a swift in this sentence? | A fast horse | *A bird | A person's name | A quick reply
exercise: «Taylor Swift re-recorded her early albums.» Why does Swift start with a capital letter? | It is the start of a sentence about speed | It means very fast | *It is a person's name | It is a bird's name
test: «Python for quick scripts, Swift and Kotlin for phone apps.» In this sentence, Swift is | A singer's name | Very fast | A bird | *A computer language for making phone apps
test: «Gulls and swifts feast on them» in the ant nest sentence. What does swifts mean? | Fast horses | Quick replies | People who run races | *Birds that eat insects
exam: Jayden says that in «swifts scream over the chimneys», swifts must mean fast things. What is the best answer? | Yes, because the word starts with a capital letter | *No, the chimneys and screaming show the swifts are birds, so context gives the right meaning | Yes, swift always means fast, so the sentence is about speed | No, swifts are never in a sentence about chimneys
